        pages: [
          {
            title: 'FilicÄƒu',
            subtitle: 'The Transylvanian Partnership Trick-Taker',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "FilicÄƒu (also known as FilkÃ³ or FlÄƒcÄƒu) is a classic trick-taking partnership game from the Transylvania region of Romania. It belongs to the venerable Schafkopf family of games and is distinct for its use of a 32ndcard Germanndsuited 'William Tell' pack. The name 'FilicÄƒu' translates to 'unmarried boy,' a nickname given to the Over-Knaves which serve as the game's highest trumps. The game is highly aggressive, with a scoring system focused exclusively on capturing Aces and Tens to avoid the shameful status of 'Slaves'.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Originating among the multi-ethnic communities of Transylvania, FilicÄƒu is a regional adaptation of German Schafkopf. The use of the William Tell deckâ€”where the Aces represent the four seasonsâ€”is a hallmark of Austro-Hungarian influence in the region.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '4 players in two fixed partnerships (sitting opposite each other).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '32-card German deck. Suits: Acorns (Makk), Leaves (ZÃ¶ld), Hearts (Piros), Bells (TÃ¶k).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '32-card German deck. Suits: Acorns (Makk), Leaves (ZÃ¶ld), Hearts (Piros), Bells (TÃ¶k).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Deal all cards face down, 8 per player, proceeding anticlockwise. The dealer flips the bottom card of their hand to set the trump suit (if it's an Over-Knave, they keep flipping).",
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
